        "title": {
          "en": "The slow tortoise"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The tortoise walked slowly. The hare ran quickly.\n\"Slowly and quickly tell how they moved,\" said the teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "adverb",
          "how",
          "when"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "An adverb tells more about a verb. It tells how, when or where. In She sings sweetly the word sweetly tells how she sings.\nMany adverbs end in ly: slowly, quickly, loudly, happily. Some tell time such as today and soon.\nAn adjective describes a noun and an adverb describes a verb. A quick runner uses quick for the noun; runs quickly uses quickly for the verb."
        }
